<%# The official metadata an admin sets on a form, and what the sidebar's
    Advanced Search facets on. Shared by the create wizard and the edit page so
    the two can never offer different fields.

    These describe the form; none of them gate it. Who may see a form is the
    ACL's business alone, so tagging a form to an agency narrows a search
    without ever taking the form away from anybody.

    Locals:
      f         the form builder
      template  the Forms::Template being edited (a new one on create) %>
<div class="form-group">
  <label for="form_form_number">Form Number</label>
  <%= f.text_field :form_number,
                   id: "form_form_number",
                   class: "form-control",
                   maxlength: 30,
                   placeholder: "e.g. HR-101" %>
  <small class="form-text" style="color: #6c757d;">
    The official number printed on the form, if it has one. People search by it.
  </small>
</div>

<div class="form-group">
  <label for="form_form_type">Form Type</label>
  <%= f.select :form_type,
               options_for_select(Forms::Template::FORM_TYPES, template.form_type),
               { include_blank: "Not set" },
               { id: "form_form_type", class: "form-control" } %>
</div>

<div class="form-group">
  <label for="form_description">Description</label>
  <%= f.text_area :description,
                  id: "form_description",
                  class: "form-control",
                  rows: 2,
                  maxlength: 500,
                  placeholder: "e.g. Request time off for a qualifying medical or family event." %>
  <small class="form-text" style="color: #6c757d;">
    One line saying what the form is for. Shown when searching and matched on,
    so it is the easiest way to make a form findable.
  </small>
</div>

<div class="form-group">
  <label>Owning Organization</label>
  <small class="form-text" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; color: #6c757d;">
    Which part of the county issues this form. Used for searching only — it does
    not control who can see or submit it.
  </small>
  <%= render "shared/org_cascade",
             param_scope: "form_template",
             labels: { agency: "Not set", division: "Not set",
                       department: "Not set", unit: "Not set" },
             selected: { agency: template.agency_id, division: template.division_id,
                         department: template.department_id, unit: template.unit_id } %>
</div>
